Most of us don't lack creative ideas. Think about the last time. you solved a problem in an unexpected way. Maybe you figured out a shortcut at work or improvised a meal from the leftovers in your fridge. We don't always label those everyday moments as creative, though. Instead, we think of creativity as making art or music, and we assume that it's something you're born with, not something you can cultivate. But psychologists' research suggests that creativity isn't just about flashes of brilliance or artistic talent. It's about how we approach problems, respond to challenges and turn our ideas into reality.
